"overall-explanation"><p><br></p><p><code><strong>The Microsoft Azure Recov=
ery Services (MARS) agent</strong></code> is <strong>correct</strong>. To e=
nsure that your 20 on-premises servers running Windows Server are backed up=
 daily and that all files and folders are included in these backups, while =
also maintaining three copies of the backups in Azure it's best to set up t=
he Microsoft Azure Recovery Services (MARS) agent on your servers. The MARS=
 agent is like a dedicated backup assistant for your servers. It allows you=
 to plan daily backups, making sure all your important files, folders, and =
even the system state from on-premises machines and Azure VMs are securely =
saved. This provides an additional level of protection for your data.It als=
o supports keeping multiple copies of these backups in Azure, and it's cost=
-effective.<br></p><p><code><strong>The Azure Site Recovery Mobility servic=
e</strong></code> is <strong>incorrect</strong>. It is primarily used for d=
isaster recovery and migration scenarios. Its main role is to efficiently r=
eplicate entire virtual machines and physical servers to Azure, which is es=
sential for maintaining business continuity during major disasters. However=
, when it comes to routine tasks like backing up individual files and folde=
rs every day, it lacks the level of control. For your daily backup needs, w=
here the focus is on protecting all your files and folders, maintaining mul=
tiple copies, and doing so cost-effectively, the Microsoft Azure Recovery S=
ervices (MARS) agent is the better-suited option.<br></p><p><code><strong>V=
olume Shadow Copy Service (VSS)</strong></code> is <strong>incorrect</stron=
g>. VSS is like a tool in Windows that helps to take snapshots of your file=
s and folders. These snapshots are like pictures of your data at a specific=
 moment. You can recover items if you accidentally delete something by goin=
g back to that snapshot and retrieving what you lost. While VSS is helpful =
for backups, it doesn't offer the same level of automation, integration wit=
h Azure services and cost-effectiveness as the Microsoft Azure Recovery Ser=
vices (MARS) agent. Using VSS for daily backups would require more manual e=
ffort and scripting to fulfill the specified requirements.</p><p><br></p><p=
