g> because enterprise applications in Microsoft Entra ID provide a framewor=
k for enabling SAML-based single sign-on (SSO). By integrating your line-of=
-business (LOB) application as an enterprise application, you can enable SA=
ML SSO to authenticate users seamlessly using their Entra credentials. Ente=
rprise applications allow you to configure SSO and manage access to cloud o=
r on-premises applications.</p><p><br></p><p><code><strong>Conditional Acce=
ss policies</strong></code> is <strong>correct</strong> because Conditional=
 Access policies allow you to enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) bas=
ed on specific conditions, such as access attempts from unknown locations. =
Conditional Access policies evaluate signals like user location, device com=
pliance, and risk level to enforce security controls. In this scenario, enf=
orcing MFA for users accessing the application from unknown locations can b=
e easily implemented through Conditional Access.<br></p><p><code><strong>Az=
ure Application Gateway</strong></code> is <strong>incorrect</strong> becau=
se Azure Application Gateway is a Layer 7 load balancer that manages applic=
ation traffic and web application firewall (WAF) features. It does not prov=
ide SAML SSO or enforce MFA. It is used for load balancing, not identity ma=
nagement or access control.<br></p><p><code><strong>Microsoft Entra Privile=
ged Identity Management (PIM)</strong></code> is <strong>incorrect</strong>=
 because PIM is designed to manage and secure privileged access to resource=
s. It focuses on assigning and monitoring privileged roles, not enabling SA=
ML SSO or enforcing MFA for users accessing an application.<br></p><p><code=
><strong>Microsoft Entra ID Protection</strong></code> is <strong>incorrect=
</strong> because Entra ID Protection identifies and mitigates risky sign-i=
n attempts and user accounts. While it provides risk-based Conditional Acce=
ss features, it is not directly responsible for enforcing SAML SSO or confi=
guring MFA based on location-specific conditions. Conditional Access polici=
es are more appropriate for the described use case.</p><p><br></p><p><stron=
g>Read More:</strong></p><ul><li><p><a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/=
